{{- /*
Context polix injects at session start, agent neutral, as the agent reads it. The header line goes first when any
switch of guidance in polix.yaml is on, followed by the "- " items of each switch turned on, with no blank lines;
the whole text is trimmed, and it is empty when every switch is off. Each line is concise and at most 120
characters with the default folders (a test checks it): split a rule into several items rather than wrap it.
Data: .Commit, .Edit and .Layout (the switches), .Rules, .Plans and .Reports (the folders, relative to the root,
without a trailing slash).
*/ -}}
{{- if or .Commit .Edit .Layout}}
This project is managed by polix.
Follow these rules:
{{- end}}
{{- if .Commit}}
- Run each git commit as a command of its own: never chain it with &&, ; or |, nor wrap it in sh -c or bash -c.
- Pass the commit message with -m, -F or a heredoc inside -m.
- Otherwise polix does not recognise the commit and skips its pre_commit gates.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Edit}}
- Create and change files only with the edit tool of the agent: polix checks only the edits made through it.
- Never write files from the shell: no sed -i, perl -i, > or >>, tee, heredocs or scripts that write files.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Layout}}
- Use these folders, set in polix.yaml, and no other paths:
  - {{.Rules}}/: the rules on how to write the code, one yaml file per topic.
  - {{.Plans}}/: the implementation plans, one per file.
  - {{.Reports}}/: the reports of audits and reviews, one per file.
{{- end}}
